3.x -> 4.x (PHP 8.1 modernization)

> This section is a historical record of the 4.x release, which was never published.
> Its `Amazon\SNS` replacement advice is **stale**: 5.x removed the whole AWS surface
> (see the 4.x → 5.x section above), so those SNS classes no longer exist. Use the APNs
> HTTP/2 or FCM HTTP v1 provider APIs directly.

1. Backward Incompatible Changes
2. New Features

========================================
1. Backward Incompatible Changes
========================================

- PHP: minimum supported version is now `>= 8.1` (was `>= 7.4`).
- Adapter contract (`BackQ\Adapter\AbstractAdapter`):
  - Methods now declare return types. Subclasses/consumers overriding any of
    `connect`, `disconnect`, `bindRead`, `bindWrite`, `pickTask`, `putTask`,
    `ping`, `hasWorkers`, `setWorkTimeout`, `afterWorkSuccess`,
    `afterWorkFailed` must declare compatible (covariant) return types.
  - `pickTask($timeout = null): bool|array` (was untyped)
  - `putTask($body, $params = []): string|int|bool` (was untyped)
  - `ping($reconnect = true): bool` (was untyped)
  - `hasWorkers($queue): bool|int|null` (was untyped; the `$queue` argument is
    now required by the contract, children may keep a default)
  - `connect(): bool`, `disconnect(): bool`, `bindRead($queue): bool`,
    `bindWrite($queue): bool`, `afterWorkSuccess($workId): bool`,
    `afterWorkFailed($workId): bool` (were declared `: void` and contradicted
    every concrete implementation — this previously failed to load on PHP 8)
  - `setWorkTimeout(?int $seconds = null): void` (was untyped)
- `BackQ\Worker\AbstractWorker::$workTimeout` is no longer typed `int` (it is
  plain untyped, default `null`). Child classes must not declare an `int`
  (or `?int`) type for a property they inherit.
- `BackQ\Adapter\Redis\Queue::$retryAfter` / `$blockFor` are untyped (matched
  to the vendored `Illuminate\Queue\RedisQueue` parent).
- `BackQ\Message\Guzzle::$request` is untyped (holds the string form; a psr7 v1
  `Request` object has no `__toString`).
- `BackQ\Message\Amazon\SNS\Application\PlatformEndpoint\PublishMessageInterface::getMessage()`
  is now `: string`.
- `BackQ\Message\Guzzle` now serializes requests via
  `GuzzleHttp\Psr7\Message::toString()` and parses with
  `Message::parseRequest()` (psr7 &ge; 2.7; the `str()`/`parse_request()`
  function shims were removed in psr7 v2).
- Dependency floors raised: `symfony/process` `^5.4 | ^6.4 | ^7.0`,
  `guzzlehttp/psr7` `^2.7`, `psr/log` `^1.1 | ^2.0 | ^3.0`,
  `illuminate/queue`/`illuminate/redis` `^10`. `opis/closure` stays `^3.6`
  (4.x removes the public `SerializableClosure` constructor that
  `BackQ\Message\Closure` relies on).
- Legacy APNs binary protocol support is **removed** (Apple deprecated the
  protocol long ago; APNs stopped supporting the legacy binary interface on
  port 2195). The following classes are deleted, as is the entire
  `duccio/apns-php` dependency:
  - `BackQ\Adapter\ApnsdPush`
  - `BackQ\Worker\Apnsd`
  - `BackQ\Publisher\Apnsd`
  - `BackQ\Message\ApnsPHP`
  - `BackQ\Logger` no longer implements `ApnsPHP_Log_Interface` (its
    `log($sMessage, $debug = false)` API is unchanged).
  - The `example/workers/apnsd.php` and `example/publishers/apnsd.php` examples
    are removed.
  - Replacement: the APNs HTTP/2 provider API, or AWS SNS via
    `BackQ\Publisher\Amazon\SNS\Application\PlatformEndpoint\Publish` /
    `BackQ\Worker\Amazon\SNS\Application\PlatformEndpoint\Publish`.
- Legacy GCM/FCM push support is **removed** (Google shut down GCM in 2019; the
  code built on the ZF1 `Zend_Mobile_Push_*` classes, which are no longer
  shipped). The `Zend_Mobile_Push` dependency is dropped and the following
  classes are deleted:
  - `BackQ\Adapter\Fcm`
  - `BackQ\Message\Fcm`
  - `BackQ\Worker\Fcm`
  - `BackQ\Publisher\Fcm`
  - Replacement: the FCM HTTP v1 API, or AWS SNS FCM platform endpoints via
    `BackQ\Publisher\Amazon\SNS\Application\PlatformEndpoint\Publish` /
    `BackQ\Worker\Amazon\SNS\Application\PlatformEndpoint\Publish`.

========================================
2. New Features
========================================

- Test suite added under `tests/` (PHPUnit 10, `composer app-tests`), with
  coverage of adapters, workers, publishers and messages.
- Constructor property promotion: `BackQ\Adapter\Redis`, `BackQ\Message\Process`,
  `BackQ\Adapter\Amazon\DynamoDb\QueueTableRow` (first param renamed `$payload`),
  `BackQ\Adapter\IO\StreamIO`.
- `str_contains` / `$e::class` / `final` class constants applied throughout
  (`BackQ\Logger`, SNS platform-endpoint workers, `BackQ\Adapter\Nsq`).

